=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/Diagnostic (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/Diagnostic   kind=page   web route=(unrouted)
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/DiagnosticPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  SchemaDriftPage / ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage do. The generated prompt's idealized "DiagnosticPage.xaml +
  DiagnosticPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/System" is mapped onto these real conventions; the C#
  namespace is TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemDiagnostics (NOT ".System", which would shadow the BCL System
  root). The surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory under route name "Diagnostic"
  (ShellWindow.xaml.cs). The web page is unrouted (it is NOT in web/src/App.tsx — confirmed; SystemPage.tsx notes
  "SystemStatusPage, ApiLogsPage, DiagnosticPage already cover"), so per the prompt's "(if routed) map (unrouted) to
  it as a deep link" it is wired only as a page-factory deep-link seam and is deliberately NOT added to RouteTable.cs
  (which mirrors App.tsx and is guarded by NavigationTests).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the two manifest data sources are useRunDiagnostic (POST /system/diagnostic) and
  formatDiagnosticReportText. (1) useRunDiagnostic is a MUTATION — the web page intentionally never auto-runs on
  mount (the endpoint fans out concurrent probes and is rate-limited), so DiagnosticPageViewModel.RunAsync is fired
  ONLY by the Run/Re-run affordance and the empty-state CTA; it reads through an injected IDiagnosticRunner. The
  default EmptyDiagnosticRunner (the un-wired shell registration, matching every sibling W7 page's
  Empty<X>Feed.Instance host-injection precedent) leaves the surface on its empty state and only surfaces the error
  panel if pressed with no contract client; the generated-client-backed DiagnosticClientRunner
  (DiagnosticPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI operation post_api_v1_system_diagnostic (no params, no
  body), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches the view; an ApiException surfaces the failure
  panel exactly as the web onError path does. (2) formatDiagnosticReportText is ported 1:1 as the pure
  DiagnosticReportText.Format (the Download .txt body) and asserted byte-for-byte by ReportText_matches_the_web_plain_text_format.
- The web page renders all of its regions INSIDE the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as
  visible Fluent regions per ADR-006: the failed-run error panel (TsGlassPanel, danger border + glyph, layered over
  whatever is below — never hidden), the overall hero (status glyph circle + verdict + generated-at + a check-count
  TsBadge), the Copy report (TsCopyButton over the report JSON) + Download .txt (TsButton) actions, the per-check
  cards (one TsGlassPanel each: status glyph + name + id + detail + optional remediation block + status TsBadge +
  duration), the in-flight TsSpinner panel, and the TsEmptyState panel with a Run CTA. Never a blank region. The
  Download uses DownloadsFolderReportDownloader (DownloadsFolder.CreateFileAsync + FileIO.WriteTextAsync), the native
  analogue of the web blob download, behind the injectable IDiagnosticReportDownloader.
- SI units N/A — the only quantities on this surface are a probe duration in milliseconds (web "{{ms}}ms", rendered
  verbatim) and a check count (i18n plural); both substitute the raw integer exactly as the web i18next interpolation
  does. The report timestamp formats through DateTimeFormatting (web formatDateTime) at the display boundary.
- i18n: all 16 manifest keys (plus the diagnostic.overall.* / diagnostic.status.* the page also resolves) already
  existed verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (the generator emitted them from web en.json). The catalog
  realized the check-count plural as diagnostic.checkCount.Plural.one/.other; to make the manifest key
  diagnostic.checkCount literally present and resolvable, the plain diagnostic.checkCount ("{0} check") +
  diagnostic.checkCountOther ("{0} checks") keys were added to all three catalogs. The surface resolves every key
  through the ILocalizer facade; ar/he fall back to English by design until translated.
- Test wiring: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj Compile-links the Microsoft.UI-free sources (its documented INVARIANT —
  the case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated union). The 3 new DiagnosticPage
  Model/Source/ViewModel links were inserted in sorted position (between feature-views\DetailedStatistics.* and
  feature-views\DriveAnalyticsSection.*); the Microsoft.UI view (DiagnosticPage.cs) is excluded.

